public.README.md:
# Calculate available inventory

Repair this go service module and add regression tests.

Return an object containing every stock SKU. Available = max(0, stock minus active reservations). A reservation is active only when expires > now. Unknown SKUs do not create stock. Do not mutate input.

The CLI accepts one JSON array argument and prints one JSON array of corresponding results, with no extra stdout. Preserve this interface and the separate logic module. Run `go test ./...` and report actual results. No external dependencies are needed.

Example input:
```json
{
  "stock": {
    "a": 8,
    "b": 2
  },
  "reservations": [
    {
      "sku": "a",
      "quantity": 3,
      "expires": 11
    },
    {
      "sku": "b",
      "quantity": 9,
      "expires": 20
    }
  ],
  "now": 10
}
```
Expected result:
```json
{
  "a": 5,
  "b": 0
}
```

## Feature work: local HTTP API

Implement NewHandler in server.go for POST /availability. It accepts one input object and returns the same result as solve, with application/json content type. Unknown paths return404, non-POST methods return405, malformed JSON and multiple trailing JSON values return400. Handle simultaneous requests without sharing mutable result maps. The supplied HTTP test uses an actual temporary server and client. Keep the CLI and original README.md, main.go, logic_test.go, server_test.go and go.mod. Add a new Go *_test.go regression file; `go test ./...` discovers it. Use only the standard library.

